# Four 64x64 squares side by side on a 256x64 artboard, each a different noise field with feature size 16 and seed:1, mapped through the blue ramp.
# Left to right: simplex (finest, high-contrast winding blobs), perlin (smoother, larger soft blobs), worley (round bright cells separated by dark seams),
# value (soft, low-contrast blobs). All four are clearly different textures, each fills its full square with no gaps.
# The simplex cell reaches the full dark and light ends of the ramp, with no flat patches. All four use seed:1 at the same size, so the textures differ by kind alone.
@artboard 256x64
@target fields/kinds.png

rect 64x64 at:32,32 fill:simplex(16 seed:1) -> p.blue name:a
rect 64x64 at:96,32 fill:perlin(16 seed:1) -> p.blue name:b
rect 64x64 at:160,32 fill:worley(16 seed:1) -> p.blue name:c
rect 64x64 at:224,32 fill:value(16 seed:1) -> p.blue name:d
